From 7960815e2aca977937da036c5d0db8be4ab4bf78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sathisha S <sathisha.shivaramappa@arm.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] uefi-sct: Test authenticated KEK persistence across reset

Add an AuthVariablePersistence test to SecureBootBBTest to verify
that authenticated KEK data, attributes, and replay protection
persist across a cold reset.

The test installs a dedicated KEK using a PK-signed authenticated
update with timestamp T1 and validates the resulting variable.
It then performs a cold reset using the SCT recovery mechanism.

After reset, the test verifies that the KEK data and attributes
remain unchanged, checks that replaying the T1 authenticated
update is rejected, and confirms that a newer T2 update is
accepted.

Add the required KEK test certificate, signature list, and
authenticated update fixtures to the Secure Boot dependency
build. Update the SCT test registration, recovery integration,
and user documentation.

This improves coverage for platforms where ordinary UEFI
variables persist across reset but authenticated Secure Boot
variable state may not.

Signed-off-by: Sathisha S <sathisha.shivaramappa@arm.com>
